tion/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region II is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains two holes.\n\n- Region III is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region IV is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-98036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcec96822d528707b92d1272c067c20aa43e1855e5af75e029f0649525c347f9"} {"question" "q-98036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-98036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-98036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (2,1)}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>25}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn. \n\n- Region I is simply connected. It's a plane region (a circle) without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(2,1).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 25.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcec96822d528707b92d1272c067c20aa43e1855e5af75e029f0649525c347f9"} {"question" "q-123916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (0,0)}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\n- Region III is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123923" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcec96822d528707b92d1272c067c20aa43e1855e5af75e029f0649525c347f9"} {"question" "q-123923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the given regions is simply connected"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123923" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-124782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ge 1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,xy\\ne 0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-124782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the ellipse ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\n- Region II  is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected.  The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the coordinate axes.  Thus, the region is formed by four disjoint pieces and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-124782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcec96822d528707b92d1272c067c20aa43e1855e5af75e029f0649525c347f9"} {"question" "q-124782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-124782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-124782" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-124775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-x\\ge 0}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+x\\ne 0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-124775" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y\\ge x.$ So,   it's a plane region without holes,\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole (containing all points of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1$).\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=-x.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14