e08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region (a circle) with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1.$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123887" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcec96822d528707b92d1272c067c20aa43e1855e5af75e029f0649525c347f9"} {"question" "q-123887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "q-123887" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/state.json" "file_sha256" "ede08d08aad1f3ad08b96829d52bd4c668b5c92afb54ca304dd5705821035ba4"} {"question" "e-8682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/ef9e1dfd559c1e8818f14e100e07ab36ca167a4bd2ddf970bf3f5ef325103d64.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/example-8682.json" "file_sha256" "e6224b5f139881043761ecbd2c8edd1b3474b092e80a6d18dc755bc99ce18443"} {"question" "e-8682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/d4d61cf87f2c62c5cf4727384d6dfcc05cada6b23025dd6dd674130eaf64dd45.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/example-8682.json" "file_sha256" "e6224b5f139881043761ecbd2c8edd1b3474b092e80a6d18dc755bc99ce18443"} {"question" "e-8684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/b8e630b749cbfee41d73a620ffd284f3216bb8a43affdc26543f1eb57e4613c5.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/example-8684.json" "file_sha256" "a03f90b3c0ae0cab753df07f5b1934780c5726b74b9f731fe21e1e018d9dc12b"} {"question" "e-8684" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/example-8684.json" "file_sha256" "a03f90b3c0ae0cab753df07f5b1934780c5726b74b9f731fe21e1e018d9dc12b"} {"question" "e-9498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n- $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n\n- $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n\n- $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/example-9498.json" "file_sha256" "1451d940f4d75383dc5f8176465c2cb31210ca84a47f7c50717fe0fcd7dbed5f"} {"question" "e-9498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/assets/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x.$ So, it's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not*  simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071672/example-9498.json" "file_sha256" "1451d940f4d75383dc5f8176465c2cb31210ca84a47f7c50717fe0fcd7dbed5f"}] "usage" {"e-8682" [] "q-98032" [] "q-98035" [] "q-98036" [] "e-8684" [] "e-9498" [] "q-98033" []} "basis" 2571 "retractions" [[17592186172595 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/q-98036.png)\n\nWhich of the regions shown above are simply connected?"] [17592186171786 :question/problem "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/8bc6eee716b3c35ded2c54628da21226.png)"] [17592186171786 :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D$.\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/4c9ec6c4f35d8902525483f7a86d70af.png)"] [17592186171787 :question/problem "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/1164dfedfd68fecee2af1031295ffb86.png)"] [17592186171787 :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/06bab6e6cec4b75e4a1363b4dbc20310.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D$. In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/42d126c7bd2ac311262b659d2596dc37.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions:\n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""] [17592186171829 :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\n1. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n2. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n3. $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: \\mid \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$"] [17592186171829 :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/998c3fae4e98a4fcb65db22d9a3b178a.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D$. In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3357/Source/Images/06500334cbe214f995d2491dc71265a1.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x$. So, it's a plane region without holes.\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0)$.\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""]] "immutable_answers" [17592186171518 17592186171519 17592186171520 17592186171521 17592186171522 17592186171524 17592186171525 17592186171526 17592186171527 17592186171528 17592186171530 17592186171531 17592186171532 17592186171533 17592186171534 17592186171536 17592186171537 17592186171538 17592186171539 17592186171540] "immutable_fields" [[17592186171517 :answer-field/correct] [17592186171517 :answer-field/id] [17592186171517 :answer-field/key] [17592186171517 :answer-field/type] [17592186171523 :answer-field/correct] [17592186171523 :answer-field/id] [17592186171523 :answer-field/key] [17592186171523 :answer-field/type] [17592186171529 :answer-field/correct] [17592186171529 :answer-field/id] [17592186171529 :answer-field/key] [17592186171529 :answer-field/type] [17592186171535 :answer-field/correct] [17592186171535 :answer-field/id] [17592186171535 :answer-field/key] [17592186171535 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
